# Week 7 Expectations

## 1. Secure Coding Practices
The application follows secure coding standards to prevent unauthorized access and secure API communication.

## 2. Proper Authentication
JWT authentication is implemented for validating users before accessing APIs.

## 3. Proper Authorization
Role-based authorization is implemented to provide controlled access to APIs.

## 4. API Protection
All sensitive APIs are protected using Spring Security configurations.

## 5. Endpoint Testing
Endpoints are tested using Postman with:
- Valid token
- Invalid token
- Missing token
- Different user roles

## 6. Messaging Validation
Kafka or RabbitMQ messaging is tested successfully using producer and consumer communication.
